  ],
  "text": "Every breath you take is plant waste. You eat food. A plant builds it from things you could never eat. Three ingredients. Sunlight, water, and the carbon dioxide already in the air. Light hits the leaf and splits the water apart. That is the hard part done. Then the carbon is pulled from the air and assembled into sugar. And the oxygen left over is not the point of any of this. It gets thrown out. Every plant on Earth has been dumping it into the air for two billion years. You are alive because of a waste problem that nothing ever bothered to fix. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
